  After CTS (r1): design area 5.08 mm^2 (69 % of the block incl.
  macros); setup WNS -0.06 ns at 40 ns (reg-to-reg, before routing).
  The CPU's wire demand is the problem: 28.3 m of global route for
  1.90 mm^2 of cells (crypto: 8.9 m for 1.07 mm^2).

== Top level, v1 dry run (provisional block abstracts from 4_cts)
  synth/floorplan/PDN/place/CTS complete: block power pins connect
  (389 PDN-0110 warnings, all on the OpenRAM macros' own 0.49 um met4
  supply columns that the abstract also lists; the 1.6 um straps over
  them get via4). GRT: 79,305 overflowed gcells (met1 34,105, met2
  39,974) - the ~400 nets from the CPU's 2900 um top edge had to reach
  die pins sideways through a 90 um channel, and GRT spread them over
  both blocks where only met5 is free. Fixed by the v2 floorplan.

